! SASE averaged-vs-unaveraged comparison deck (see README.md, "SASE").
!
! Same 1D CLARA-like beam and undulator as deck.in - rho = 0.005,
! aw = 1.012, gamma_r = 456.4, planepole - but started from shot noise
! instead of a seed, and run far enough to saturate.  Everything that
! run_compare_sase.py does not set is fixed here, so the only differences
! between a pair of runs are the solver mode, the mesh and the step.
!
! q_noise = .true. and no seed file: the field starts at zero and grows
! out of the beam's own shot noise.  That is the point of the deck - a
! seeded flat-top cannot discriminate cell size or exercise what
! averaging gives up (bandwidth, harmonics, coherent spontaneous
! emission), and every averaged validation before this one was seeded.
!
! iRandSeed fixes the shot-noise realisation.  The default (-1) seeds the
! RNG from the system clock, which would make an averaged-vs-unaveraged
! comparison meaningless.  init_random_seed (random.f90) folds
! tProcInfo_G%rank into the seed, so a fixed iRandSeed only reproduces the
! realisation at a fixed number of MPI ranks - run_compare_sase.py asserts
! that the two runs used the same rank count.
!
! sFModelLengthZ2 = 110 holds the 50-long bunch plus the ~21 of slippage
! over 340 periods plus headroom, so the radiation never reaches the mesh
! end and setup_calcs never has to extend the mesh for us.  sBeta is inert
! here (the absorber lives in the diffraction step, which qDiffraction =
! .false. switches off), so the NBZ2_G node-count problem of the 3D deck
! does not arise.
!
! qFilter is likewise inert without diffraction, so the unaveraged run
! carries its full resolved spectrum - harmonics included - while the
! averaged run carries one band about the carrier.  Compare the
! fundamental band, not total power.

&MDATA
 qOneD                  = .true.
 qFieldEvolve           = .true.
 qElectronsEvolve       = .true.
 qElectronFieldCoupling = .true.
 qFocussing             = .false.
 qDiffraction           = .false.
 qFilter                = .true.
 q_noise                = .true.
 qUndEnds               = .false.
 beam_file              = 'sase_beam.in'
 sElectronThreshold     = 0.05
 iNumNodesX             = 1
 iNumNodesY             = 1
 nodesPerLambdar        = 12
 sFModelLengthX         = 4.0
 sFModelLengthY         = 4.0
 sFModelLengthZ2        = 110.0
 iRedNodesX             = 1
 iRedNodesY             = 1
 sFiltFrac              = 0.3
 sDiffFrac              = 1.0
 sBeta                  = 0.0
 seed_file              = ''
 srho                   = 0.005
 sux                    = 1.0
 suy                    = 1.0
 saw                    = 1.0121809
 sgamma_r               = 456.40
 lambda_w               = 0.0275
 Dfact                  = 0.0
 zundType               = 'planepole'
 taper                  = 0.0
 lattFile               = ''
 iRandSeed              = 1
 stepsPerPeriod         = 30
 nPeriods               = 340
 sZ0                    = 0.0
 iWriteNthSteps         = 1000000
 iWriteIntNthSteps      = 1000000
 sPEOut                 = 0.0
 /
